{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Re-measured before/after on a QUIET machine (matched conditions, same commands), superseding the earlier numbers which were taken while other work contended for the 3 cores:\n\n| `-n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300` | wall | CPU (user+sys) | largest test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| origin/main | 82.39s | 137.49s | three fills: 40.62s / 40.50s / 38.40s |\n| this change | **33.47s** | **55.51s** | **17.72s** |\n\nWall **-59%**, CPU **-60%**, largest test **-56%**. 11 passed both ways. The 'before' figure came from checking out the origin/main version of the file into this same worktree and venv, so the only variable is the change itself.\n\nPatch set 2 folds in both advisory findings from the LLM code review of patch set 1, since both are genuine defects in code this change introduces:\n\n1. *Digest overstated its guarantee.* `_corpus_digest` keyed on the pandoc binary PATH and `st_size` only, so the docstring claim that 'a stale render can never be served' did not hold for two same-size builds. Now a `_pandoc_stamp()` helper reports `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()` alongside path and size — the version is what actually decides the output, which is why the `wiki` extra pins `pypandoc-binary==1.15` at all — and the docstring states the real strength ('a strong practical key rather than a proof'). The version probe costs one ~0.18s subprocess per session.\n\n2. *A slow winner could delete another worker's lock.* The deadline path used to `rmdir` the lock before rendering locally, so worker A (slow, still alive) could have its lock stolen by B, acquired by C, and then removed by A's own `finally` — two workers holding nominally the same lock. The deadline path no longer touches the lock at all: it just renders locally. Only the creator ever removes the directory, so removal by name is now unambiguous. Cost of the stricter rule is that a genuinely SIGKILLed winner leaves the lock for the session and each other worker waits its 150s once before rendering locally — still inside the 300s guard, and strictly safer than the steal.\n\nVerified after the amendment: 11 passed, all gates green, `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786605770142968001,"uuid":"161c4940-8a50-41ea-ba5f-3e35ae712ec0"}